The main weakness in group H is that the rule uses a budget-first (“earliest maintenance”) ordering for mid-horizon decisions, which can over-concentrate work on a few robots and force extra openings, while also leaving less room for useful deviations. I change H (same duty length, multiple types) to a balanced count-first ordering, but with a secondary preference for robots closer to maintenance so maintenance events stay staggered. E and M keep their existing behavior.

