## Task
Write a rule based on a clearly DIFFERENT idea from all rules above, likely to score higher.

response:
The rule uses a maintenance-return horizon idea: it triggers a robot’s maintenance mainly when that maintenance can still finish and contribute before the horizon, and otherwise defers near-end maintenance while balancing load. New robot types are selected by a near-end bin-packing estimate (fewer remaining shifts / less overshoot) or by long-run throughput cost with a consolidation penalty for already-opened types. The default action is separated from the ordering of the remaining available robots, which deliberately alternates between maintenance-urgent and load-balanced alternatives so sparse genome deviations explore useful tradeoffs.

