The main change targets the H group: when several robot types have the same duty length, the previous rule’s budget-first sorting and maintenance-avoidance logic over-staggered maintenance and raised imbalance. For those equal-duty multi-type instances I fall back to the decoder’s naturally balanced reuse order (fewest duties first, then most remaining budget), while making the default new-robot choice prefer fit and more duties per maintenance rather than the genome’s gene type. E and M keep the prior logic, which already performed well.

