response:
The rule uses a two-regime idea: for homogeneous duty lengths it follows congestion-aware fair rotation, while for mixed duty lengths it switches to maintenance-paced sequencing—using last-duty robots first when safe, otherwise protecting capacity by avoiding near-maintenance robots and balancing normalized load. New robot types are chosen by horizon fit and efficiency for homogeneous cases, but mixed cases give the genome’s type gene a strong role so random deviations can explore useful type mixes; near the end, exact/least-overshoot coverage dominates.

