## Task
Write a rule based on a clearly DIFFERENT idea from all rules above, likely to score higher.

response:
The rule uses a capacity-aware “balanced earliest-deadline” bias: it prioritizes finishing robots whose maintenance cycle is nearly exhausted only when a maintenance window is safe, otherwise it preserves fresh capacity, and among equally urgent robots it levels combined count/hour load. Alternative robot orders complement the default choice so random deviations can explore the opposite maintenance/balance trade-off, while new robot types are chosen by cost-per-duty-hour with fit and already-opened-type penalties.

